      { id: 3, question: 'What does statelessness mean in REST?', options: ['Server cannot maintain sessions', 'Each request contains all information needed to process it', 'API cannot have a database', 'Clients cannot send state in bodies'], correctIndex: 1, explanation: 'Statelessness means each request must contain all information needed to process it — the server stores no client context between requests.' }
