      { id: 2, question: 'Which compression format offers the best ratio and is supported by all modern browsers?', options: ['gzip', 'deflate', 'br (Brotli)', 'lz4'], correctIndex: 2, explanation: 'Brotli (br) offers 15-25% better compression than gzip and is supported by all modern browsers. It is ideal for text-based assets.' },
      { id: 3, question: 'What is the purpose of rate limiting?', options: ['Speed up responses', 'Protect APIs from abuse by limiting request frequency', 'Compress responses', 'Cache API responses'], correctIndex: 1, explanation: 'Rate limiting restricts how many requests a client can make in a given time period, preventing abuse and ensuring fair usage.' }
