        content: 'Effective WebSocket connection management tracks connection lifecycle and resource allocation. On connection establishment, authenticate the client using a token from the initial HTTP upgrade request or a first message. Store connection metadata (user ID, rooms, capabilities) in a Map keyed by connection ID. Implement connection limits per user — allow 3-5 concurrent connections to support multiple devices while preventing abuse. Heartbeat mechanisms detect dead connections faster than TCP keep-alive. Send ping frames every 30 seconds and close connections that do not receive pong within 10 seconds. Track connection state with a state machine: CONNECTING, CONNECTED, RECONNECTING, DISCONNECTED. Broadcast connection status to other clients when presence matters (chat applications). Handle backpressure — if the client cannot consume messages fast enough, buffer messages with a maximum size and drop oldest when full. Implement graceful shutdown: send a close frame with reason code, wait for acknowledgment, then terminate the TCP connection. Clean up all server-side resources (rooms, subscriptions, timers) on disconnect to prevent memory leaks.'
