        content: 'Robust reconnection handles network disruptions without overwhelming servers. Exponential backoff increases delay after each failed attempt: delay = min(baseDelay * 2^attempt + jitter, maxDelay). Start with 1 second, doubling to a maximum of 30 seconds. Jitter (random variation) prevents thundering herd when many clients reconnect simultaneously: delay = delay + random(0, 1000ms). Implement a maximum retry count — after 10-15 failed attempts, stop reconnecting and prompt the user to check their connection. Cache the last received message ID to resume from where the connection dropped — the server can replay missed messages. Connection state broadcasting keeps the UI informed: this.status$ = new BehaviorSubject(\'disconnected\'). Display visual indicators (reconnecting spinner, connection status badge) to maintain user trust. Socket.io provides built-in reconnection with reconnectionDelay, reconnectionDelayMax, and reconnectionAttempts configuration. For raw WebSocket reconnection, implement it in the close event handler: ws.onclose = (event) => { if (!event.wasClean) { setTimeout(reconnect, calculateDelay()); } }. Handle network state changes with navigator.onLine and the online/offline events to trigger immediate reconnection when connectivity returns.'
